# herdr-pr-tracker configuration.
#
#   cp config.example config
#
# `config` is gitignored. The plugin reads two locations: the repo root, then
# the plugin config dir, which wins:
#
#   herdr plugin config-dir herdr-pr-tracker
#
# Every setting is commented out at its default. `KEY=value`, one per line. A
# matched pair of single or double quotes around a value is stripped.
#
# The pane reads this file once, at startup, and a plugin reload does not
# restart the pane process. After an edit, close the widget:
# `herdr plugin pane close <pane-id>`.
#
# Signal precedence, sort order and the meaning of each mark are fixed.

# Seconds between GitHub polls. A poll costs the same however many PRs come
# back.
#POLL_SECONDS=60

# The GitHub search for the authored view, e.g. add `user:acme` to narrow it to
# one org. It does not reach the inbound view. To watch other people's PRs, use
# the inbound view (toggle it from the pane header), not `review-requested:@me`
# here: this view would render those rows as yours.
#SEARCH_QUERY="is:pr is:open author:@me archived:false"

# Repositories and owners to exclude from both views. Separate entries with
# spaces or commas. Matching ignores case.
#
#   IGNORE_REPOS="acme/web-app acme/metrics-service"
#
#   acme/web-app   one repository
#   acme/          every repository under one owner
#   web-app        an ERROR: dropped
#
# GitHub answers a qualifier with no owner by subtracting nothing, with no
# error, so the plugin refuses a bare name instead of guessing.
#
# A dropped entry shows at the foot of the list as `⚠ 2 bad IGNORE_REPOS
# entries`. To see which entries, run `bun bin/pane.ts` by hand: it names them
# on stderr.
#
# The search subtracts ignored PRs, so they cost no MAX_PRS budget and the pane
# never counts them. A typo in a well-formed entry subtracts nothing and gives
# no warning. Each entry adds a negated qualifier to every search; GitHub
# accepted forty. A list GitHub refuses shows as a failed refresh in the pane
# header.
#IGNORE_REPOS=""

# Authors whose pull requests are never fetched, in either view. Same
# separators, case rule, dedup and `⚠` count as IGNORE_REPOS.
#
#   IGNORE_AUTHORS="octocat renovate[bot] app/dependabot"
#
#   octocat          a user login
#   renovate[bot]    a bot login, with its suffix
#   app/dependabot   a GitHub App, the same as dependabot[bot]
#   @octocat         an ERROR — dropped
#   acme/web-app     an ERROR — dropped (that is IGNORE_REPOS)
#
# A bot needs its `[bot]` suffix or the `app/` prefix. GitHub reports
# Dependabot's login as `dependabot`, but `-author:dependabot` subtracts nothing
# and reports no error. A bare bot name is also a valid user login, so the
# parser cannot catch it.
#IGNORE_AUTHORS=""

# Hide PRs with no update in this many days, in both views. Unset, 0, or a
# non-number keeps every PR.
#
#   MAX_IDLE_DAYS=30
#
# "Update" is GitHub's `updated` date: a comment, push, review, label, bot
# comment or CI run counts. The age on each row is the time since the PR
# opened, so a row can read `200d` and still pass. The search subtracts hidden
# PRs, so `✓ all clear` can still leave idle PRs open. The cutoff is a UTC date.
#MAX_IDLE_DAYS=

# Maximum PRs fetched in one request (GitHub's search page cap is 100). The
# "+N older" row counts the PRs beyond this.
#MAX_PRS=100

# auto | always | never. `auto` shows the owner only when a PR's owner differs
# from the one most of your PRs share.
#SHOW_OWNER=auto

# Set to 0/off/false/no to render without colour. `COLOUR` also works, and
# `COLOR` wins if you set both.
#COLOR=on

# unicode | nerd. The set of marks the pane and the sidebar draw. Both sets mark
# the same facts in the same cells.
#
# `unicode` needs no font installed, but most monospace fonts lack its marks
# (Monaco has one of the eleven), so OS font fallback draws them from mixed
# typefaces.
#
# `nerd` draws GitHub's Octicons from the Nerd Fonts private-use block, and
# gives a review verdict and a build result separate marks. It needs a font
# that has them:
#
#   Ghostty      nothing to do: it embeds Symbols Nerd Font 3.4.0
#   iTerm2       brew install --cask font-symbols-only-nerd-font, then
#                Profiles > Text > "Use a different font for non-ASCII text"
#   elsewhere    any patched Nerd Font as the terminal font
#
# A missing glyph is a blank cell, so check the pane after you switch. Write
# the name in lower case: the plugin ignores an unknown name and keeps the
# default.
#GLYPHS=unicode

# Minimum seconds between sidebar-token lookups for one pane. Each lookup runs
# two `gh` subprocesses.
#TOKEN_THROTTLE_SECONDS=30
